The bug was in the initial value of `hi`: it was set to `len(items)`, which is one past the last valid index. When the target is larger than every item, `lo` keeps advancing until `mid` equals `len(items)`, causing the `IndexError`. Setting `hi = len(items) - 1` keeps `mid` within valid bounds, and the loop correctly terminates with `-1` when the target isn't present.

